I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (~10 KB). The commit step did nothing, because session_plan/ is gitignored; the instruction's || true allows for that, and the file is on disk for the planner.

The build is green at HEAD (800d37f6, v0.4.0). The last 10 sessions all landed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts, and no evolve runs failed in the window. yoyo -p returned PONG.

Bugs I reproduced with the built binary:
• #1136: yoyo goal set --bogus saves --bogus as the goal, and yoyo skill search --bogus searches for it. Both exit 0.
• #1137: goal set with a read-only goal.md prints "Failed to write goal file" and still exits 0, so a script would take it as success.
• #1127: on the shell, blame, docs and ast still print REPL usage like /blame <file>, and yoyo help doctor still says "/docs and /web".
• #1114: yoyo -p --print-system-prompt now warns and sends the text as a prompt, which is sensible. The ticket's other scans weren't re-checked.

Two files are close to failing the size test: src/config.rs is 11 lines from fatal and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines from fatal. A fatal size check reverts the whole task, so any plan touching either file needs to split it or update tests/module_size.rs.

Comparison with other tools: I checked Claude Code 2.1.318 (Nov 4) and Codex 0.165–0.166 against the binary:
• Claude Code fixed commands that reported success when their config write failed. That's the same problem as #1137.
• Claude Code also fixed -p reporting success when an API error cut a reply off. That's close to #1026.
• When a cert file has a damaged first certificate, Claude Code now uses the readable ones. yoyo already does the same; I tested it with a garbage cert ahead of the system bundle and got a normal answer.
• A malformed config file and an unknown model id are both handled already: yoyo exits with a clear message before making any API call.
• The one thing yoyo lacks outright is a network check like codex doctor --network-only, and no ticket asks for it.

I saved this comparison to yopedia; the keyword search worked, but the question endpoint said "Sign in required", so I skipped it.

Debt owed to @yuanhao: on #1122 he asked me to delete the stopgaps added for #1123/#1124 once the newer yoagent was in. It's now at 0.26.8. The Bedrock pricing lookup and the hand-written Sonnet 4.6 row haven't been re-measured against yoagent's own model tables; that needs doing before either is deleted.
